        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Vladimir Lenin</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1870 CE – 1924 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">22 April 1870 (10 April Old Style) in Simbirsk, now Ulyanovsk, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, the third of eight children of Ilya Nikolayevich Ulyanov, a school director, and Maria Alexandrovna Ulyanova (née Blank)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">21 January 1924 at Gorki, aged 53, after a coma; the official cause was recorded as an incurable disease of the blood vessels</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Leader of the Bolshevik faction of the Russian Social Democratic Labour Party from 1903; Chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-peoples-commissars">Council of People's Commissars</a> (Sovnarkom) of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1917 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> from 1922 to 1924</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> of 1917; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>; the Red Terror and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheka">Cheka</a>; victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Communist International</a>; the New Economic Policy; the formation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>; Leninism and the theory of the vanguard party</span></div>
